    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Trea Turner** (78.64) and **Kyle Schwarber** (77.46) serving as the clear anchors of the offense. Both benefit immensely from a high-leverage matchup against V\u00e1squez, whose 4.75 xERA provides a significant +18% SP skill boost to our projections. With **Trea Turner** slotting into the two-hole and **Kyle Schwarber** leading off, their combined efficiency is maximized by their order positioning. **Yordan Alvarez** also remains a premier play (74.26) despite a neutral matchup, as his elite 0.454 xwOBA profile remains too potent to fade. Meanwhile, **Junior Caminero** (63.30) provides strong middle-of-the-order value, benefiting from a favorable platoon advantage against Flaherty that helps offset a slight park penalty.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the marginal range, specifically **Casey Schmitt** (38.76). While **Casey Schmitt** held appeal due to a potential #1 order slot, he fell just short of our 40.0 efficiency floor due to a poor park factor and a -14% penalty against the SP\u2019s skill set, leading us to favor the higher baseline projections of **Carson Benge** (44.85) and **Luke Raley** (46.89). We are keeping a close eye on **Carson Benge** and **Luke Raley** as their official lineups remain pending; should those lineups shift disadvantageously, we risk sub-optimal production in those slots. Additionally, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (50.01) remains a high-risk, high-reward play: while his elite sprint speed is vital for our pursuit of the SB category, the combination of a difficult matchup against Jump and a -15% platoon penalty suggests that his value is strictly tethered to his base-running volatility rather than raw hitting efficiency.",
